Subject: [PATCH] layout: add Finnish å/ä/ö to the latin layouts

wvkbd ships no Finnish layout and cannot be given one from the outside.
`--list-layers` offers sixteen layers, and every one that names a language
is a non-Latin script (cyrillic, arabic, persian, greek, georgian,
hebrew). Every Latin-script language shares `full`, which is US QWERTY:
the compiled keymap contains no adiaeresis, odiaeresis or aring at all.

Hyprland's `input:kb_layout` cannot fix this either. wvkbd uploads its
own keymap over zwp_virtual_keyboard_v1, so the compositor's layout
setting has no bearing on what the on-screen keyboard emits.

Upstream's answer today is the compose key: Cmp then `a` opens a panel
with à á â ã ä å, and Cmp then `o` has ö. That is three interactions per
character in a language where ä and ö are ordinary letters, not accents —
"näytä" needs it twice. On a lockscreen, where the keyboard is the only
input device the machine has, it is worse than tedious.

So put them on dedicated keys, in the positions a physical FI board uses:
å right of p, ö and ä right of l.

── why Copy and not Code ─────────────────────────────────────────────────

Copy keys carry a unicode codepoint and upload a temporary keymap on
press (keyboard.c, `case Copy`), which is how every compose-layer key in
this file already emits these exact characters — keys_compose_a has ä and
å, keys_compose_o has ö, all as Copy. Reusing that costs nothing and
leaves keymap.mobintl.h untouched. Adding real scancodes instead would
mean hand-editing the embedded xkb keymap to claim spare keycodes, for a
gain (autorepeat on ä) that no one holding a tablet will notice.

The shift variant rides in code_mod, matching the compose-layer entries:
0x00E4/0x00C4 for ä, 0x00F6/0x00D6 for ö, 0x00E5/0x00C5 for å.

── why the 0.5 pads are dropped ──────────────────────────────────────────

kbd_init_layout normalises each row independently — `k->w = (width /
rowlength) * k->width`, with rowlength recomputed at every EndRow — so a
row can hold any total and the keys simply divide it. Rows here already
disagree (landscape runs 13/13/13/12).

The 0.5 pads either side of the home row exist to centre nine keys under
ten. With ö and ä the row holds eleven, is no longer narrower than the
row above, and the centring padding is what would push it off. Dropping
both pads is what keeps the two rows in column.

Landscape keeps its trailing 0.5 pad: å goes before it, between p and
Tab, so the row stays 14.0 against the home row's 14.5.

── replacing rather than adding a layer ──────────────────────────────────

A Finnish layout is US QWERTY plus three keys, so patching `full`,
`fullwide` and `landscape` in place costs no US capability — nothing is
removed and no extra step enters the NextLayer cycle. A separate `finnish`
layer would mean pressing the layer key before every ä.

Not upstreamable as-is for that reason: upstream would want this behind a
new layer, not folded into the default latin layouts.

--- a/layout.mobintl.h
+++ b/layout.mobintl.h
@@ -207,9 +207,9 @@ static struct key keys_full[] = {
   {"i", "I", 1.0, Code, KEY_I, &layouts[ComposeI]},
   {"o", "O", 1.0, Code, KEY_O, &layouts[ComposeO]},
   {"p", "P", 1.0, Code, KEY_P, &layouts[ComposeP]},
+  {"å", "Å", 1.0, Copy, 0x00E5, 0, 0x00C5},
   {"", "", 0.0, EndRow},

-  {"", "", 0.5, Pad},
   {"a", "A", 1.0, Code, KEY_A, &layouts[ComposeA]},
   {"s", "S", 1.0, Code, KEY_S, &layouts[ComposeS]},
   {"d", "D", 1.0, Code, KEY_D, &layouts[ComposeD]},
@@ -219,7 +219,8 @@ static struct key keys_full[] = {
   {"j", "J", 1.0, Code, KEY_J, &layouts[ComposeJ]},
   {"k", "K", 1.0, Code, KEY_K, &layouts[ComposeK]},
   {"l", "L", 1.0, Code, KEY_L, &layouts[ComposeL]},
-  {"", "", 0.5, Pad},
+  {"ö", "Ö", 1.0, Copy, 0x00F6, 0, 0x00D6},
+  {"ä", "Ä", 1.0, Copy, 0x00E4, 0, 0x00C4},
   {"", "", 0.0, EndRow},

   {"⇧", "⇫", 1.5, Mod, Shift, .scheme = 1},
@@ -281,9 +282,9 @@ static struct key keys_full_wide[] = {
   {"i", "I", 1.0, Code, KEY_I, &layouts[ComposeI]},
   {"o", "O", 1.0, Code, KEY_O, &layouts[ComposeO]},
   {"p", "P", 1.0, Code, KEY_P, &layouts[ComposeP]},
+  {"å", "Å", 1.0, Copy, 0x00E5, 0, 0x00C5},
   {"", "", 0.0, EndRow},

-  {"", "", 0.5, Pad},
   {"a", "A", 1.0, Code, KEY_A, &layouts[ComposeA]},
   {"s", "S", 1.0, Code, KEY_S, &layouts[ComposeS]},
   {"d", "D", 1.0, Code, KEY_D, &layouts[ComposeD]},
@@ -293,7 +294,8 @@ static struct key keys_full_wide[] = {
   {"j", "J", 1.0, Code, KEY_J, &layouts[ComposeJ]},
   {"k", "K", 1.0, Code, KEY_K, &layouts[ComposeK]},
   {"l", "L", 1.0, Code, KEY_L, &layouts[ComposeL]},
-  {"", "", 0.5, Pad},
+  {"ö", "Ö", 1.0, Copy, 0x00F6, 0, 0x00D6},
+  {"ä", "Ä", 1.0, Copy, 0x00E4, 0, 0x00C4},
   {"", "", 0.0, EndRow},

   {"⇧", "⇫", 1.5, Mod, Shift, .scheme = 1},
@@ -1114,13 +1116,13 @@ static struct key keys_landscape[] = {
   {"i", "I", 1.0, Code, KEY_I, &layouts[ComposeI]},
   {"o", "O", 1.0, Code, KEY_O, &layouts[ComposeO]},
   {"p", "P", 1.0, Code, KEY_P, &layouts[ComposeP]},
+  {"å", "Å", 1.0, Copy, 0x00E5, 0, 0x00C5},
   {"", "", 0.5, Pad, .scheme = 1},
   {"Tab", "Tab", 1.0, Code, KEY_TAB, .scheme = 1},
   {"", "", 0.0, EndRow},

   {"↑", "↑", 0.75, Code, KEY_UP, .scheme = 1},
   {"↓", "↓", 0.75, Code, KEY_DOWN, .scheme = 1},
-  {"", "", 0.5, Pad, .scheme = 1},
   {"a", "A", 1.0, Code, KEY_A, &layouts[ComposeA]},
   {"s", "S", 1.0, Code, KEY_S, &layouts[ComposeS]},
   {"d", "D", 1.0, Code, KEY_D, &layouts[ComposeD]},
@@ -1130,6 +1132,8 @@ static struct key keys_landscape[] = {
   {"j", "J", 1.0, Code, KEY_J, &layouts[ComposeJ]},
   {"k", "K", 1.0, Code, KEY_K, &layouts[ComposeK]},
   {"l", "L", 1.0, Code, KEY_L, &layouts[ComposeL]},
+  {"ö", "Ö", 1.0, Copy, 0x00F6, 0, 0x00D6},
+  {"ä", "Ä", 1.0, Copy, 0x00E4, 0, 0x00C4},
   {"'", "\"", 1.0, Code, KEY_APOSTROPHE, &layouts[ComposeBracket]},
   {"/", ">", 1.0, Code, KEY_SLASH},
   {"", "", 0.0, EndRow},
